      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. so if i'm trying to keep my levels steady, what are some actual food examples of high vs low GI? like what should i avoid and what should i eat instead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are some examples of high and low GI foods:\n\nHigh GI foods to limit or avoid:\n- White bread and sugary snacks (GI: 80-100)\n- Refined grains like white rice and pasta (GI: 70-80)\n- Sugary drinks and desserts (GI: 90+)\n- Fresh fruit, especially tropical fruits like mango and pineapple (GI: 50-60)\n\nLow GI foods to prioritize:\n- Whole grains like brown rice, quinoa, and whole wheat bread (GI: 20-30)\n- Non-starchy vegetables like broccoli, cauliflower, and leafy greens (GI: 10-30)\n- Legumes like lentils, chickpeas, and black beans (GI: 30-50)\n- Most non-tropical fruits like apples, berries, and citrus fruits (GI: 30-50)\n\nKeep in mind that the GI value can vary depending on the specific food and serving size.",
